##### Decision Variables

For each $i \in S$, $j \in C$:

\[
x_{ij} \geq 0
\]

where $x_{ij}$ is the quantity shipped from supplier $i$ to customer $j$ (continuous).

##### Objective

\[
\min \sum_{i \in S} \sum_{j \in C} c_{ij} x_{ij}
\]

##### Constraints

1. **Demand satisfaction** (each customer receives at least its demand):

\[
\sum_{i \in S} x_{ij} \geq d_j \qquad \forall j \in C
\]

2. **Supply capacity** (each supplier does not exceed its capacity):

\[
\sum_{j \in C} x_{ij} \leq s_i \qquad \forall i \in S
\]

3. **Non-negativity**:

\[
x_{ij} \geq 0 \qquad \forall i \in S,\, j \in C
\]

##### Summary of Sets

\[
\begin{aligned}
S &= \{S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, S6, S7, S8, S9, S10\} \\
C &= \{C1, C2, C3, C4, C5, C6, C7, C8, C9, C10\}
\end{aligned}
\]

##### Complete Model

\[
\begin{aligned}
\min_{x_{ij} \geq 0} \quad & \sum_{i \in S} \sum_{j \in C} c_{ij} x_{ij} \\
\text{s.t.} \quad
& \sum_{i \in S} x_{ij} \geq d_j \qquad \forall j \in C \\
& \sum_{j \in C} x_{ij} \leq s_i \qquad \forall i \in S \\
& x_{ij} \geq 0 \qquad \forall i \in S,\, j \in C \\
\end{aligned}
\]

